1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,570
Section 1

2
00:00:01,570 --> 00:00:02,449
SUSIE:

3
00:00:02,449 --> 00:00:02,960
Hello?

4
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:03,944
PAUL:

5
00:00:03,944 --> 00:00:05,853
Hi, Susie, it's Paul here.

6
00:00:05,853 --> 00:00:07,001
How are you?

7
00:00:07,001 --> 00:00:08,797
Enjoying your new job?

8
00:00:08,797 --> 00:00:11,940
You're working at the library, aren't you?

9
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:12,434
SUSIE:

10
00:00:12,434 --> 00:00:12,928
Yes.

11
00:00:12,928 --> 00:00:17,372
I started when the library re-opened a month ago.

12
00:00:17,372 --> 00:00:18,360
It's great.

13
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:18,698
PAUL:

14
00:00:18,698 --> 00:00:22,760
Actually Carol and I have been meaning to join for a while.

15
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:23,177
SUSIE:

16
00:00:23,177 --> 00:00:24,426
Oh, you should.

17
00:00:24,426 --> 00:00:26,092
It doesn't cost anything,

18
00:00:26,092 --> 00:00:29,841
and the new library has all sorts of facilities.

19
00:00:29,841 --> 00:00:33,590
It's not Just a place where you borrow books.

20
00:00:33,590 --> 00:00:38,228
For instance, there's an area with comfortable seats where you can sit

21
00:00:38,228 --> 00:00:40,934
and read the magazines they have there.

22
00:00:40,934 --> 00:00:43,640
Some people spend the whole morning there.

23
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:44,041
PAUL:

24
00:00:44,041 --> 00:00:44,442
Mmm.

25
00:00:44,442 --> 00:00:48,050
Wish I had that amount of time to spend!

26
00:00:48,050 --> 00:00:48,452
SUSIE:

27
00:00:48,452 --> 00:00:53,680
Yes, you must be pretty busy at present, with the children and everything?

28
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:54,076
PAUL:

29
00:00:54,076 --> 00:00:55,264
We are, yes.

30
00:00:55,264 --> 00:00:58,433
But we're hoping to get away this summer.

31
00:00:58,433 --> 00:01:00,810
We're thinking of going to Greece.

32
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:01,165
SUSIE:

33
00:01:01,165 --> 00:01:06,129
Well, we've got a much larger section of the library devoted to travel books

34
00:01:06,129 --> 00:01:06,483
now,

35
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:09,320
so you should come and have a look.

36
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:13,319
I can't remember if there's anything specifically on Greece,

37
00:01:13,319 --> 00:01:15,540
but I should think so.

38
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:15,936
PAUL:

39
00:01:15,936 --> 00:01:16,332
OK.

40
00:01:16,332 --> 00:01:21,481
Now Carol's organising a project for the history class she teaches at school -

41
00:01:21,481 --> 00:01:25,442
it's about life in the town a hundred years ago.

42
00:01:25,442 --> 00:01:28,610
Do you have anything that might be useful?

43
00:01:28,610 --> 00:01:29,078
SUSIE:

44
00:01:29,078 --> 00:01:36,566
Yes, actually we've now got a new section with materials on the history of the town

45
00:01:36,566 --> 00:01:37,970
and surrounding region.

46
00:01:37,970 --> 00:01:38,354
PAUL:

47
00:01:38,354 --> 00:01:38,737
Right.

48
00:01:38,737 --> 00:01:39,888
I'll tell her.

49
00:01:39,888 --> 00:01:44,107
You can't always find that sort of thing on the internet.

50
00:01:44,107 --> 00:01:49,476
Now in the old library there used to be a separate room with reference

51
00:01:49,476 --> 00:01:49,860
books.

52
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:52,810
It was a really nice quiet room.

53
00:01:52,810 --> 00:01:53,192
SUSIE:

54
00:01:53,192 --> 00:01:58,153
Yes, We've put those books in the main part of the library now,

55
00:01:58,153 --> 00:02:01,970
but we do have a room called the community room.

56
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:04,511
It can be hired out for meetings,

57
00:02:04,511 --> 00:02:08,140
but at other times people can use it to study.

58
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:08,523
PAUL:

59
00:02:08,523 --> 00:02:10,054
I might use that.

60
00:02:10,054 --> 00:02:13,500
It's hard to find anywhere quiet at home sometimes.

61
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:13,893
SUSIE:

62
00:02:13,893 --> 00:02:17,825
I can't remember how old your son and daughter are ...

63
00:02:17,825 --> 00:02:22,151
we've introduced a special section of fiction written specially for teenagers,

64
00:02:22,151 --> 00:02:25,690
but they might be a bit young for that?

65
00:02:25,690 --> 00:02:26,160
PAUL:

66
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:28,040
Yes, they would be.

67
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:28,456
SUSIE:

68
00:02:28,456 --> 00:02:32,620
Well, we do have lots of activities for younger children.

69
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:33,435
PAUL:

70
00:02:33,435 --> 00:02:34,250
Yes?

71
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:34,648
SUSIE:

72
00:02:34,648 --> 00:02:37,432
For example we have a Science Club.

73
00:02:37,432 --> 00:02:43,002
At the next meeting, they're going to be doing experiments with stuff that everyone

74
00:02:43,002 --> 00:02:46,980
has in the kitchen - sugar and flour and so on.

75
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:47,462
PAUL:

76
00:02:47,462 --> 00:02:49,870
They might be interested, yes.

77
00:02:49,870 --> 00:02:50,278
SUSIE:

78
00:02:50,278 --> 00:02:54,362
And we have a competition for children called Reading Challenge.

79
00:02:54,362 --> 00:02:58,445
That doesn 't begin until after the end of term.

80
00:02:58,445 --> 00:03:00,895
They have to read six books,

81
00:03:00,895 --> 00:03:04,570
and they get a certificate if they manage it.

82
00:03:04,570 --> 00:03:04,929
PAUL:

83
00:03:04,929 --> 00:03:09,961
So that gives them something to do while they're on holiday, instead of getting

84
00:03:09,961 --> 00:03:10,320
bored.

85
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:10,774
SUSIE:

86
00:03:10,774 --> 00:03:12,135
That's the idea.

87
00:03:12,135 --> 00:03:15,310
And there's special activities for adults too.

88
00:03:15,310 --> 00:03:21,662
On Friday we have a local author called Tanya Streep who's going to be

89
00:03:21,662 --> 00:03:23,930
talking about her new novel.

90
00:03:23,930 --> 00:03:29,789
It's called 'Catch the Mouse' and she based the story on a crime that

91
00:03:29,789 --> 00:03:32,300
actually took place here years ago.

92
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:32,673
PAUL:

93
00:03:32,673 --> 00:03:33,046
Right.

94
00:03:33,046 --> 00:03:34,910
We're not free on Friday,

95
00:03:34,910 --> 00:03:37,520
but I'll look out for the book.

96
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:37,979
SUSIE:

97
00:03:37,979 --> 00:03:40,736
Now this probably isn't for you,

98
00:03:40,736 --> 00:03:44,870
but we do have IT support available for members.

99
00:03:44,870 --> 00:03:45,211
PAUL:

100
00:03:45,211 --> 00:03:49,990
We get quite a few older people coming along who are want ing to

101
00:03:49,990 --> 00:03:52,380
get up to speed with computer technology.

102
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:56,586
It's on Tuesday mornings - they don't need to make an appointment

103
00:03:56,586 --> 00:03:58,880
or anything, they just turn up.

104
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:03,120
PAUL:Well , my mother might be interested, I'll let her know.

105
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:03,592
SUSIE:

106
00:04:03,592 --> 00:04:04,064
OK.

107
00:04:04,064 --> 00:04:09,257
And there's another service which you wouldn't expect from a library,

108
00:04:09,257 --> 00:04:12,090
which is a free medical check-up.

109
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:17,324
The hospital arranges for someone to come along and measure the level of sugar

110
00:04:17,324 --> 00:04:18,445
in your blood,

111
00:04:18,445 --> 00:04:21,810
and they check cholesterol levels at the same time.

112
00:04:21,810 --> 00:04:22,575
PAUL:

113
00:04:22,575 --> 00:04:23,340
Really?

114
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:23,850
SUSIE:

115
00:04:23,850 --> 00:04:24,360
Yes,

116
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:27,420
but that's only for the over-60s,

117
00:04:27,420 --> 00:04:29,460
so you wouldn't qualify.

118
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:29,904
PAUL:

119
00:04:29,904 --> 00:04:30,347
OK.

120
00:04:30,347 --> 00:04:34,340
Well, I'll tell my mother, she might be interested.

121
00:04:34,340 --> 00:04:34,813
SUSIE:

122
00:04:34,813 --> 00:04:36,234
What other information ...

123
00:04:36,234 --> 00:04:42,862
well , we do have a little shop with things like wallcharts and greetings cards,

124
00:04:42,862 --> 00:04:47,596
and also stamps so you can post the cards straightaway,

125
00:04:47,596 --> 00:04:49,490
which is really useful.

126
00:04:49,490 --> 00:04:49,869
PAUL:

127
00:04:49,869 --> 00:04:50,248
Yeah.

128
00:04:50,248 --> 00:04:54,794
Well, I'll bring the children round at the weekend and we'll join.

129
00:04:54,794 --> 00:04:59,720
Oh, one more thing - I'll be bringing the car, is there parking available?

130
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:00,150
SUSIE:

131
00:05:00,150 --> 00:05:00,580
Yes.

132
00:05:00,580 --> 00:05:04,450
and it's free in the evening and at weekends.

133
00:05:04,450 --> 00:05:05,131
PAUL:

134
00:05:05,131 --> 00:05:05,813
Perfect.

135
00:05:05,813 --> 00:05:09,220
Well , thanks , Susie see you ...
